ver the long run.","p_chg":"Across 86 complete years: Casper's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.28 to \u22120.05), about \u22121.4\u00b0F since 1940. Casper's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.34\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.20 to +0.47), about +2.9\u00b0F since 1940.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months; 6 months fell. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Casper's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.18 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 12.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1982 (20.48 in); the driest, 2020 (5.79 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 28 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}